<mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Arrow colours&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;font color=&quot;#2563EB&quot;&gt;■ blue = users in (HTTPS, WebSocket)&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#1E7F3E&quot;&gt;■ green = private AWS calls through endpoints (IAM role, no keys, no internet)&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#7E57C2&quot;&gt;■ purple = internet, through the NAT gateway&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#B45309&quot;&gt;■ brown = database&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#6B7280&quot;&gt;┄ grey dashed = platform: ECS fetches secrets and the image when a task starts, logs, alarms, deploys&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;One call, step by step&lt;/b&gt;: ① staff or caller → firewall → load balancer · ② load balancer → brain (/v1 API and the live-call WebSocket) · ③ brain → NAT gateway → Sarvam (speech in and out; the only call that leaves AWS) · ④ brain → interface endpoint → Bedrock (masked text → intent, wording) · ⑤ brain → interface endpoint → SageMaker (question → search vectors and scores) · ⑥ brain → RDS (call record, KB passages, mock bank) · ⑦ brain → S3 gateway endpoint → S3 (KB files, encrypted recordings)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontColor=#1B1F24;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="160" y="1085" width="1340" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
